 "sources": [
  "Malaria 2024: ~610,000 deaths, ~95% in Africa, ~75% of African deaths under 5; spread by female Anopheles (WHO fact sheet): https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/malaria",
  "Snakebite: 5.4M bites, 81,410-137,880 deaths/yr, ~3x as many amputations/disabilities; NTD listing 2017 (WHO): https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/snakebite-envenoming",
  "India ~58,000 snakebite deaths/yr 2000-2019, mostly rural (Suraweera et al. 2020, eLife): https://elifesciences.org/articles/54076",
  "Saw-scaled viper stridulation and India's Big Four (cobra, krait, Russell's viper, saw-scaled viper): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echis_carinatus ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_four_(Indian_snakes)",
  "Rabies: dogs cause 99% of human cases, 100% fatal once symptoms appear, vaccine-preventable, ~40% of deaths under 15, tens of thousands of deaths/yr, wash wound 15 min; Zero by 30 (WHO): https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/rabies",
  "Chagas: ~8M infected, >10,000 deaths/yr, triatomines bite face at night and infect via feces (WHO): https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/chagas-disease-(american-trypanosomiasis) ; kissing bugs in southern US (CDC): https://www.cdc.gov/chagas/about/index.html",
  "Shark bites 2025: 65 unprovoked bites, 9 unprovoked fatalities (ISAF, Florida Museum): https://www.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/shark-attacks/yearly-worldwide-summary/",
